s general anesthesia in distal radius fractures in patients over 60&#x02009;years in trauma emergency</article-title><source>Anesthesiology and pain medicine</source><year>2017</year><volume>7</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>e40619</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">28920036</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="other">Committee ICCoFaD. Fracture and dislocation classification compendium&#x02014;2018. Journal of orthopaedic trauma. 2018;32.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>PQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Noffsinger</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hematoma block of distal forearm fractures. Is it safe?</article-title><source>Orthop Rev</source><year>1991</year><volume>20</volume><issue>11</issue><fpage>977</fpage><lpage>979</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1749663</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chung</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kotsis</surname><given-names>SV</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Predictors of functional outcomes after surgical treatment of distal radius fractures</article-title><source>The Journal of hand surgery</source><year>2007</year><volume>32</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>76</fpage><lpage>83</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jhsa.2006.10.010</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17218179</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bear</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Friel</surname><given-na